      "lines": [
        "Encoder: Preparing the Input",
        "• Bidirectional GRUs (types of RNNs), where input is fed forward and backward",
        "and then their hidden states are concatenated into a final hidden state",
        "• Note: each hidden state tends to summarize only closer inputs",
        "• What advantages do bi-directional RNNs have to uni-directional RNNs?",
        "• Information from the past and future contribute to predictions: e.g., can resolve for",
        "\"Teddy is a …?” if Teddy refers to a “bear” or “former US President Roosevelt”",
        "• What are disadvantages of bi-directional RNNs?",
        "• Entire sequence must be observed (e.g., unsuitable for text prediction)",
        "https://towardsdatascience.com/understanding-bidirectional-rnn-in-pytorch-5bd25a5dd66"
      ]
    },
